{
  "children": [
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Crystallite size and lattice strain in sol–gel ZnO nanoparticles from X-ray diffraction line-profile analysis",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Title"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "D. Crystal, E. Rietveld",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Author"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "ZnO nanoparticles were synthesised by a sol–gel route and calcined at 400–800 °C. Powder X-ray diffraction confirms single-phase wurtzite (P6₃mc). Crystallite sizes obtained from the Scherrer equation (14–46 nm) are compared with a Williamson–Hall analysis that separates size and microstrain contributions to the line broadening.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Abstract"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "XRD · Scherrer · Williamson–Hall · ZnO · nanoparticles",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Keywords"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Line broadening in powder diffraction carries information on both the size of coherently scattering domains and on inhomogeneous strain ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "klug1974"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Separating the two requires analysing the angular dependence of the broadening.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Theory",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Bragg's law relates the interplanar spacing ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "d_{hkl}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the diffraction angle:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "n\\lambda = 2 d_{hkl} \\sin\\theta.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:bragg",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "For a hexagonal lattice with parameters ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "a",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "c",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ",",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\frac{1}{d_{hkl}^2} = \\frac{4}{3}\\,\\frac{h^2+hk+k^2}{a^2} + \\frac{l^2}{c^2}.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:hex",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Scherrer equation estimates the mean crystallite size ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "D",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " from the instrument-corrected integral breadth ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\beta",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ":",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "D = \\frac{K\\lambda}{\\beta\\cos\\theta},\\qquad \\beta = \\sqrt{\\beta_{\\text{obs}}^2 - \\beta_{\\text{inst}}^2},",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:scherrer",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "with shape factor ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "K = 0.9",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Including a microstrain ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\varepsilon",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " gives the Williamson–Hall relation",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\beta\\cos\\theta = \\frac{K\\lambda}{D} + 4\\varepsilon\\sin\\theta,",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:wh",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "so that a plot of ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\beta\\cos\\theta",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " vs ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "4\\sin\\theta",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " has intercept ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "K\\lambda/D",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and slope ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\varepsilon",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Methods",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Zinc acetate dihydrate (0.5 M) dissolved in ethanol at 60 °C; diethanolamine added 1:1 as stabiliser.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Gel dried at 120 °C for 12 h and ground in an agate mortar.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Calcined 2 h in air at 400, 600 or 800 °C (5 °C/min).",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "XRD: Cu Kα₁ (λ = 1.5406 Å), 2θ = 20–80°, step 0.01°, LaB₆ (NIST SRM 660c) for instrumental broadening.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Results",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "rows": [
        [
          "(hkl)",
          "2θ (°)",
          "d (Å)",
          "FWHM 400 °C (°)",
          "FWHM 800 °C (°)"
        ],
        [
          "(100)",
          "31.77",
          "2.814",
          "0.612",
          "0.198"
        ],
        [
          "(002)",
