        ]
      ],
      "caption": "Indexed reflections of wurtzite ZnO.",
      "label": "tab:peaks",
      "alignment": "lrrrr",
      "style": "booktabs",
      "type": "Table"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Refined lattice parameters at 800 °C are ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "a = 3.2498(3)\\ \\text{Å}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "c = 5.2066(5)\\ \\text{Å}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", giving ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "c/a = 1.602",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", close to the ideal ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\sqrt{8/3} = 1.633",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "rows": [
        [
          "Calcination (°C)",
          "D Scherrer (nm)",
          "D W–H (nm)",
          "ε (×10⁻³)",
          "R²"
        ],
        [
          "400",
          "14.2",
          "17.8",
          "2.41",
          "0.962"
        ],
        [
          "600",
          "26.5",
          "29.3",
          "1.12",
          "0.978"
        ],
        [
          "800",
          "45.8",
          "48.1",
          "0.37",
          "0.954"
        ]
      ],
      "caption": "Size and strain from Eqs. (4) and (5).",
      "label": "tab:size",
      "alignment": "lrrrr",
      "style": "booktabs",
      "type": "Table"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Discussion",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Scherrer sizes are systematically smaller than W–H values because the Scherrer approach attributes all broadening to size. The strain relaxes by a factor of six on calcination, consistent with annealing of grain-boundary defects. Grain growth follows",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "D^n - D_0^n = k_0\\, t\\, \\exp\\!\\left(-\\frac{Q}{RT}\\right),",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:growth",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "and with ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "n = 2",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " we obtain ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "Q \\approx 48\\ \\text{kJ mol}^{-1}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Conclusion",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Line-profile analysis of sol–gel ZnO shows crystallite growth from 18 to 48 nm and strain relief between 400 and 800 °C. Values from Scherrer and W–H converge once strain becomes negligible.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "text": "\\begin{thebibliography}{99}\n\\bibitem{klug1974} H. P. Klug and L. E. Alexander, \\emph{X-Ray Diffraction Procedures}, 2nd ed. (Wiley, 1974).\n\\end{thebibliography}",
      "type": "RawLatex"
    }
  ],
